Title: review_notes: notes append fails with Argument list too long on a large request
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-11-09T14:41Z reviewer created

--- body ---

## Context
Found by raid 632b19 on PR #2312 (ticket 1480, `git rm --cached` of 1,085 files): gaze_setup
crashed in `review_notes.open_review` → `request` → `_write` with `OSError: [Errno 7] Argument
list too long: 'git'`. `_write` (scripts/review_notes.py:741-747) passes the whole JSON entry as
`git notes append -m <line>`; the request's `what` field carries the request-pull diffstat, so a
request over a large diff exceeds the OS argument limit. `keep_head` ran before the failing
write, leaving the review head ref without its request entry. No review record exists for #2312,
so its gate cannot run: the defect blocks a merge.

## Plan
Pass the entry through stdin: `git notes append -F - <anchor>` with `stdin=line` (the `_git`
helper already takes `stdin`). Red test first in tests/test_review_notes.py: open a review whose
request `what` is ~300 KB (monkeypatch `_request_what`), assert the entry reads back whole.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `open_review` on a request whose entry exceeds the argument limit writes it and reads it back whole
- [ ] the new test fails on main for `OSError: Argument list too long` and passes with the fix
- [ ] `make check` passes
